WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.517
Draw a dot in the middle of a blank page. Imagine you're standing on that dot, on a corner you walk past every day.

00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:14.136
Stay still and listen for the nearest sound. I can hear a bicycle bell just to my left, so I'll mark a little circle beside the dot.

00:00:14.136 --> 00:00:20.098
Now listen beyond the corner. A bus is idling a block away. Its hum goes near the edge of my page.

00:00:20.098 --> 00:00:27.496
When the bicycle passes, I draw an arrow from left to right. The bell and the bus are on the same map, but only one of them is moving.

00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:34.763
Come back at a different hour and use a fresh page. Lay the two maps side by side and look for a sound that appears on only one of them.
